+## RequestBodyLimitMiddleware
+
+Buffers HTTP request bodies before calling the application and rejects bodies
+that exceed a configured limit. The limit counts received bytes, regardless of
+`Content-Length`. Oversized requests receive a plain-text `413` response with
+the body `Request body too large`; the application is not called and later
+chunks are not read.
+
+```python
+from starlette.applications import Starlette
+from starlette.middleware import Middleware
+from starlette.middleware.body_limit import RequestBodyLimitMiddleware
+
+
+app = Starlette(middleware=[Middleware(RequestBodyLimitMiddleware, max_bytes=1024)])
+```
+
+`max_bytes` must be `None` or a non-negative integer. Invalid values, including
+booleans, raise `ValueError` at construction. `None` disables buffering and the
+limit. A zero limit accepts empty bodies. WebSocket and lifespan scopes pass
+through without buffering.
+
+Accepted bodies are replayed to the application, so request body and JSON
+helpers work normally, including repeated cached reads. Subsequent receive
+calls are delegated to the original receive channel.
+
 ## BaseHTTPMiddleware
 
 An abstract class that allows you to write ASGI middleware against a request/response
